# ci/setup-build-box.sh is read verbatim and handed to cloud-init as user_data
# by ci/provision-build-box.py, so it runs as bash on Ubuntu no matter which
# machine checked it out. A Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true would rewrite
# it to CRLF, and every line would reach the box with a trailing \r — which bash
# reports as "command not found" on lines that are plainly correct. Pin it.
*.sh text eol=lf
